+zai-cron-agent-478334, lease 21:31Z). Zero production mutation. All facts below are
+byte-exact or API-verbatim, captured 2026-10-29T21:31–21:58Z via the MCP Control Tower
+(zero-credential plane).
+
+## Headline
+
+The "CI red on supremeai-core main" cited by #2597/#2225 as the prime root-cause
+candidate decomposes into **two independent structural defects plus one cosmetic red**:
+
+1. **Push-CI on `main` is structurally dead** — the workflow trigger filter is corrupted
+   to `branches: ain]` (byte-exact; `[main]` minus its leading `[m`). Valid YAML, wrong
+   branch: every push to `main` since the corruption has run **zero** CI jobs.
+2. **The nightly "🔧 PyErrorFix Engine" job has never succeeded** — 5/5 schedule runs
+   red since 10-25, including on commits whose push-run was green. Its detect/fix step
+   is `|| true`-guarded end-to-end, so the red is (by step-level elimination) the SARIF
+   upload step, not a code-quality signal.
+3. The Render build-plane burn continues in the fresh billing cycle on **two separate
+   Render accounts** (topology correction to #2597's single-view table).
+
+## F1 — push-trigger corruption (the P0 refinement)
+
+`github.read_file` on `Supremeai-bd/supremeai-core` @ HEAD `feda45e4`
+(`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, blob sha `9acd7fca32734c1ed4b1b282b6c55fa0a64634ef`,
+5422 bytes) contains, byte-exact:
+
+```yaml
+on:
+  push:
+    branches: ain]
+  pull_request:
+```
+
+- `ain]` is the scalar string `ain]` — GitHub matches it against no existing branch.
+- Mechanism: `branches: [main]` lost exactly its leading `[m` (2-char substring-eating
+  loss, consistent with a bad string-replace in an automated patch; the `autofix` job
+  holds `contents: write` + `pull-requests: write`, but no commit-history tool exists on
+  the zero-credential plane, so the introducing commit is **unproven** — flagged, not accused).
+- **Corruption window** (from `github.workflow_runs` limit=49, total_count=49):
+  - last push-event run on main: **run #39, 2026-10-27T16:53:58Z, head `832b27e`, success**
+    (= the "last green 832b27e6" of #2225/#2597);
+  - first post-corruption observation: run #40 (schedule) 2026-10-28T07:58:01Z, head
+    `feda45e` — main had advanced 832b27e→feda45e with **no push run in between**;
+  - zero push-event runs after #39 across the whole 49-run history.
+- Consequence: **main has had no test/lint/secret-scan gating since ~10-27/28**; the
+  "red CI" framing in #2597 over-states what runs: only the schedule job executes.
